@brickkit/redis-world

The reliable list queue is derived from @fantasticfour/world-redis
(https://github.com/vinnymac/worlds, packages/world-redis), licensed under
Apache-2.0. Original project: vinnymac/worlds and its contributors.

Changes: ported the queue to Workflow SDK v5's single-queue contract; added
atomic reservation and persisted attempt/delivery counters, heartbeat lease
fencing, owner-checked dedup release, capped retries without message loss,
v5 routing and binary transport, and new recovery and runtime chaos tests.
Storage, streaming, retention, and utilities are copied from the independent
@brickkit/bullmq-world v5 implementation in this repository.

The copied v5 implementation is derived from @fantasticfour/world-redis-bullmq
(https://github.com/vinnymac/worlds, packages/world-redis-bullmq), Apache-2.0.
Its v5 changes include position-based event IDs, atomic writes, restart
recovery, independent utilities, and concurrency and chaos tests.
